{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>For</b> Maroth — a place name. Some say: from the derivation of the Targum, marai shemaya, or from the root מרי. But this interpretation has no basis, for <b>she dwells</b> is a sign, upon the name of the city. And the meaning of those mentioned [cities] is that they did not go out to mourn, for they were under siege and distress, just as Ophrah was captured, and likewise." "And the meaning of <b>for it is sick</b> — from the root חיל." "And the meaning of <b>for good</b> — as those who say to me: on account that it is absent." "<b>For evil has come down</b> — the opposite of the good that she had."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Reading שלא יצאו לספוד as 'they did not go out to mourn.' The clause ושפיר at the end is rendered 'and likewise,' taking it as an adverbial conclusion, though it may alternatively refer to the city Shaphir mentioned earlier in v. 11.", 2 "The subject of נעדר ('is absent/perishing') is ambiguous; rendered impersonally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:39.468985195Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}